FILED s543m (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27), from the reviewing session's review of s543m (F2; its m-09 rows 12 13).  PRE-EXISTING: base 9a3ce86f the same.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl; scratch/s543m/p11/rows.pl prog 2):
    my $f = "/tmp/x.$$"; sub mk { open my $t, ">", $f or die; print $t "hdata"; $t } sub sz { my $s = -s $f; unlink $f; $s // "none" }
    my $hr = { fh => mk() }; %$hr = (); print "a ", sz(), "\n";
    my $ar = [ mk() ]; @$ar = (); print "b ", sz(), "\n";
    my $self = { l => [ mk() ] }; @{$self->{l}} = (); print "c ", sz(), "\n";
    package Log { sub new { bless { fh => main::mk() }, shift } sub close { my $s = shift; %$s = () } } my $lg = Log->new; $lg->close; print "d ", sz(), "\n";
    my $u; %$u = (); print "e ", ref($u), "\n";      # control: the clear VIVIFIES $u
perl: a 5 / b 5 / c 5 / d 5 / e HASH.  PCL (base and tree): a 0 / b 0 / c 0 / d 0 / e HASH.

SAME PLACE AS THE NAMED CLEAR? NO.  The named clear (`%h = ();`, s543m #5354) is `Parser2::_fh_drop_stmt_sym` (a Symbol token) -> `_fh_drop_flush_var` (the variable's CL form) -> `(p-flush-dropped-handle VAR)` emitted BEFORE the store, which READS the variable.  A dereference cannot be read that way: `%$hr` on an undef `$hr` vivifies as an lvalue but dies under strict refs as an rvalue (row e), and `@{$self->{l}}` re-evaluates an element expression.  The flush needs a PEEK through the reference (no vivify, no die, no FETCH: `%p-peek-slot` as `%p-flush-dropped-elem` uses it for the -deref kinds) of a container form evaluated once.  Direction: `_fh_drop_stmt_sym` accepts a Cast + Symbol / Cast + Block operand; the flush form peeks the referent of the operand (a plain scalar variable: read twice is safe; a block: bind once).  NOT taken in s543m (the review: not the same place; a resume begins nothing new).
